  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1029 PM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nMid-range guidance has been persistent developing an upper level low \neast of Florida on Wednesday into Thursday and there is some \nquestion as to whether this will create any rain chances for us as\nit retrogrades to the west. The ridge wants to hold on and be the\nmain weather driver in our neck of the woods, but I can't rule \nout a stray storm on Thursday.\n\nAs we get into the weekend, models are very inconsistent in \nsolution. The GFS wants to create a very wet pattern by the end of \nthe weekend and into the start of next week. In sharp contrast, the \nEuro is much more dry and holds onto some ridging influences as we \nnear the \"start\" of fall. While there were some indications last \nnight that we might start cooling off, the above normal \ntemperatures may hold on even longer.",
